{"version": 2, "width": 92, "height": 32, "timestamp": 0, "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}, "title": "pm2-liveness: a hung instance, detected and restarted"}
[0.64, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m1. Start an app with two instances\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.84, "o", "  instance 0  pid 259017  up 3s\r\n  instance 1  pid 259024  up 3s\r\n"]
[1.844, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m2. Install pm2-liveness and point it at /health\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.044, "o", "  watching /health on every instance, every 2s\r\n"]
[3.044, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m3. Break instance 1 - it returns 503 but the process stays alive\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.045, "o", "\u001b[2m$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3001/break\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.052, "o", "broken\r\n"]
[3.053, "o", "\r\n  PM2's own view, which is the whole problem:\r\n"]
[3.263, "o", "  instance 0  status online  restarts 0\r\n  instance 1  status online  restarts 0\r\n"]
[3.268, "o", "  ...both still 'online'. PM2 only sees crashes and memory limits.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36m4. pm2-liveness notices, and restarts only the broken instance\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.468, "o", "  restarting instance  app=api pm_id=1 reason=status 503\r\n"]
[5.668, "o", "  instance 0  pid 259017  up 20s\r\n  instance 1  pid 259327  up 4s\r\n"]
[5.673, "o", "\r\n  instance 1 has a new pid and a reset uptime. Instance 0 was never touched.\r\n"]
[5.673, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m5. And it is serving again\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.673, "o", "\u001b[2m$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3001/health\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.68, "o", "{\"ok\":true,\"pid\":259327}"]
[5.681, "o", "\r\n"]
